# SERIOUS-RELEASE-PRE-RELEASE-TRANCHE-01, Slice A — build-context exclusions.
#
# Purpose: keep local secrets, local databases and build noise out of the image
# layers produced by `COPY . .`.
#
# M1 REPAIR (bounded): an earlier version of this file excluded `docs/` wholesale.
# That was wrong. Runtime code reads committed JSON artifacts from
# `docs/governance/path_n_content_config/` — `engine/path_n_questions.py` (via
# `Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent / "docs" / "governance" /
# "path_n_content_config"`) and `engine/intent_serving.py` (via the relative
# `docs/governance/path_n_content_config` prefix). Excluding `docs/` would have
# shipped an image whose guided journey fails for BOTH activated domains while
# `/health` still answered 200.
#
# The exclusion is REMOVED rather than paired with a `!` re-include. Re-including
# a subtree beneath an excluded ancestor is exactly the subtlety that produced
# M1, it is the one rule whose behaviour this repository cannot currently verify
# (no Docker daemon is available here to run a real `docker build`), and getting
# it wrong reintroduces the same silent failure. An exclusion-only file has no
# such failure mode: nothing under `docs/` can be dropped by accident.
# Cost, stated rather than hidden: the image carries the repository's ~14 MB of
# documentation. That is size, not correctness, and it can be narrowed later —
# but only once a real `docker build` can prove the narrowing.
#
# Pattern note: Docker matches each pattern against the WHOLE relative path, and
# `*` does not cross `/`. A bare `*.pyc` therefore excludes only a top-level
# `.pyc`, not `engine/__pycache__/x.pyc`. Every pattern below that is meant to
# apply at any depth is written `**/…` so it does what its comment says.
#
# This file affects the Docker build context only. It changes no application
# behavior and excludes nothing the running service reads.

# Version-control and build noise.
.git
.gitignore
**/__pycache__/
**/*.pyc
**/*.bak
**/.pytest_cache/

# Local environment and any local database: never in an image layer.
**/.env
**/*.sqlite
**/*.db

# Test, benchmark and research material: not read at run time.
# `docs/` is deliberately NOT excluded (see the M1 repair note above).
# `scripts/` is deliberately NOT excluded — the backup/restore operator CLI
# (`scripts/inventorai_backup.py`, Slice E) must be runnable inside the running
# container, which is where the persistent disk is mounted.
tests/
benchmark/
benchmarks/
research/

# Local developer tooling.
verify_baseline.sh
replay_debug.txt
